course: dictionary
lesson: 6632
title: Nova: a star or a name?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and nova is one of them. In space, a nova is a star that suddenly becomes much brighter for a short time, then fades again. Nova is also a name, as in Nova Scotia, a province of Canada.
explain: The words around a word tell you which meaning is right. If the sentence is about the sky, stars or space, it means the star. If it is about a place, a zoo or a country, it is a name. «Askania-Nova helped breed wild horses» is about a place, not a star.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Askania-Nova was set up in 1898 as a nature reserve» makes sense with a place name, but not with a star. Checking like this stops you from guessing the wrong meaning.
fact: A nova is a star that suddenly becomes much brighter for a short time, then fades again.
fact: A supernova is a much bigger explosion when a star dies.
fact: Nova Scotia is a province of Canada.
fact: «Askania-Nova» is the name of a nature reserve and zoo in the Kherson region.
fact: Askania-Nova was set up in 1898 and protects one of the biggest pieces of unploughed steppe.
exercise: In space, a «nova» is a star that suddenly becomes much brighter. What is a nova? | *A star that suddenly becomes much brighter for a short time, then fades | A big piece of grassland | A kind of wild horse | A small planet with rings
exercise: «Askania-Nova helped breed wild horses in the Kherson region.» What kind of word is Askania-Nova here? | A wild horse | *A place name, a nature reserve | A star that flares up | A type of explosion when a star dies
exercise: «Nova Scotia is a province of Canada.» What is Nova here? | A star that suddenly brightens | A bigger star that dies | *Part of a place name | A zoo keeper
test: «A supernova is a much bigger explosion when a star dies.» What does supernova mean? | *A much bigger explosion when a star dies | A small rainstorm | A zoo for wild horses | A petrol station
test: «The nova flared for a few days, then faded.» What does the nova do? | Stays bright forever | Grows bigger every year | *Becomes much brighter, then fades again | Moves to another country
exam: «Askania-Nova was set up in 1898, and it keeps a big piece of steppe unploughed.» What is Askania-Nova? | *A nature reserve and zoo | A province of Canada | An explosion when a star dies | A star that flares up
